# One file, three targets, one anim chosen per target by `clip`. The scene is an ink-outlined 24x10 blue bar named box, resting at (32,32) on a 64x64 canvas.
# clip_select_spin.gif (clip:spin, 8 frames over 1s): the bar stays centered at (32,32) and turns clockwise (Undocumented, current behavior: a positive `rot` turns clockwise), horizontal in frame 1 and 11.25 degrees further each frame, reaching 78.75 degrees in frame 8 (nearly vertical); it never moves sideways.
# clip_select_slide.gif (clip:slide, 8 frames): the bar keeps its angle (horizontal) and slides right along y=32 by 2.5px per frame, from x=32 in frame 1 to x=49.5 in frame 8.
# clip_select_pose.png (clip:slide, t:.5s): a still, a single 64x64 image: the horizontal bar drawn halfway through the slide, centered at x=42, y=32.
@target anim/clip_select_{c}.gif 64x64 fps:8 dur:1s each c:[spin slide] clip:c
@target anim/clip_select_pose.png 64x64 t:500ms clip:slide

rect 24x10 at:32,32 fill:p.blue stroke:p.ink,1 name:box

anim spin dur:1s
  .box rot:key(0 90 ease:linear)

anim slide dur:1s
  .box at:key(0,0 20,0 ease:linear)

if clip == spin
  play spin
if clip == slide
  play slide
